<aside class="gm-limitations not-prose" aria-labelledby="gm-limitations-title">
  <p class="gm-limitations-eyebrow">Interpretation boundary</p>
  <h3 id="gm-limitations-title">Limitations</h3>

  <ul>
    <li>The exercises used simulated rather than real capital.</li>
    <li>
      Short-duration sessions across different cohorts and market paths do not
      constitute a repeatable performance record or controlled experiment.
    </li>
    <li>
      The strongest buy-side and sell-side results came from different dates;
      the page is a role-specific process study rather than a claim of one
      uniformly strong dual-role event.
    </li>
    <li>
      Several portal metrics and the composite weighting formula are proprietary
      or incompletely defined.
    </li>
    <li>
      Absolute P&amp;L is not directly comparable with audited real-portfolio
      performance.
    </li>
    <li>
      The 22 July event page reports 153 participants, while a manual
      ranked-list count produced 148; the asset-management P&amp;L rank is
      therefore published without a denominator.
    </li>
    <li>
      The 15 July cohort size is not documented, so its composite rank is shown
      without a denominator and is not compared mechanically with the later
      cohort.
    </li>
    <li>
      The portal uses different P&amp;L field labels across sessions, preventing
      a mechanical comparison of every buy-side financial figure.
    </li>
    <li>
      No raw transaction-level export is available for an independent
      reconstruction of the portfolios or dealer books.
    </li>
    <li>
      Average sell-side exposure was materially larger on 27 July, limiting any
      claim that the stronger output reflected uniformly lower risk.
    </li>
  </ul>
</aside>

